   "transcript": "Channel 4 Education have created a new website linked to the National Curriculum and specifically designed for schools.\nChannel 4 Education, which broadcasts more than 400 hours of innovative and thought-provoking programmes each year, is aimed at schools and learners of all ages. The programmes are enriched by a range of online, print, video and digital learning resources.\nThe new initiative was created because Channel 4 Education, working with the Victoria and Albert Museum in London, were developing a website called Every Object Tells a Story where people were invited to share stories about objects that meant something to them. Though not aimed specifically at schools, the site was relevant to key aspects of the National Curriculum and responded to needs that teachers had expressed.\nSchoolzone, which is Channel 4’s Education department, advised which areas of the National Curriculum could be related to areas of the website, and lesson plans and activity sheets were produced to link in with the programmes. Schoolzone found practising teachers who specialised in the subjects on the website and explained to them the aims and objectives of the website and the need for related lesson plans and activity sheets. Working closely with Channel 4, the teachers then wrote up the resources. We then presented the lesson plans and activity sheets to Channel 4 Education. The website was launched with the full range of worksheets, within a timescale of just four weeks."
